.TH INGOTD 8 "2026-09-07" "ingot 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ingotd \- Ingot container engine daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ingotd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ingotd
is the Ingot container engine daemon. It must run as root: it creates
namespaces, mount tables, cgroups, and firewall rules directly, with no
external runtime. Per-flag help is authoritative:
.B "ingotd \-\-help" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-data\-root " \fIPATH\fR"
Persistent state root (default \fI/var/lib/ingot\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-run\-root " \fIPATH\fR"
Runtime state root (default \fI/run/ingot\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Unix socket path (default \fI/run/ingot/ingot.sock\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-bridge " \fINAME\fR"
Default bridge interface name (default \fIingot0\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-socket\-group " \fIGROUP\fR"
Group owner for the Unix socket. Unset means mode 0600 root-only.
Anyone with socket access has effective root on the host.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
JSON config file with the same keys as the flags (docker's
\fIdaemon.json\fR equivalent). Precedence per key: CLI flag, then
config file, then built-in default. Unknown keys fail the boot.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Verbose logging.
.TP
.BR \-\-fsck
Verify image-store consistency (read-only) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-repair
Verify and repair the image store, then exit. Refuses while the
daemon is live.
.SH STARTUP
On boot the daemon reconciles persisted state: stale
.BR Running / Paused
containers are marked exited and their mounts, cgroups, veth pairs,
DNS registrations, and firewall rules are cleaned up. Unless-stopped
and always restart-policy containers are restarted. A second daemon
on the same data root is refused by an exclusive lock.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/ingot
Data root: images, containers, volumes, networks, builder cache, and
the \fIschema-version\fR marker.
.TP
.I /run/ingot/ingot.sock
API socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ingot (1),
.BR docker (8)
